WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.870
1897.

2
00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:05.250
Britain rules the largest
empire in the world.

3
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.820
Readers loved invasion stories.

4
00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:13.180
In The Battle of Dorking, from
1871, Germany invades England.

5
00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:15.460
Then Wells flips the card.

6
00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:19.200
This time, the invaders
stride in from the sky.

7
00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:23.270
So why would a British novel make
Britain the conquered country?

8
00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:27.160
In this mission, you'll see how
Wells keeps the old invasion story,

9
00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:28.930
but changes the enemy.

10
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.450
You'll read the narrator's own challenge:

11
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.840
"Are we such apostles of mercy as to
complain if the Martians warred in the same

12
00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:36.820
spirit?"

13
00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:42.140
And you'll test the novel's comparisons, from
the narrator's dodo to the artilleryman's

14
00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:44.780
"bows and arrows against the lightning".

15
00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:49.970
Your mission: explain why a British novel
makes Britain the conquered country.
